WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.140
We have three main functions in trigonometry.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.440
Three really important ones, which you will come across often.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.840
They are sine, cosine and tangent.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.020
Here's a fact, the names of all the functions in trigonometry

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.000
sounds scary.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.700
If it's the first time you are studying trigonometry,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.200
there is a very slim chance that you have heard

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.200
any of these names before.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.080
We have learnt what functions are.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.300
A function take some input

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.620
carries out a particular operation on it and gives us an output.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.400
These three names

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.360
are just fancy names given to functions. Nothing else!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.740
Let's assume, this is a sine function.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.460
Say it takes in a random value theta.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.260
It does some operation inside to give us some value.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:01:00.180
What value? What operation ? That depends entirely on the triangle.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.260
We know, that trigonometry generally deals with right triangles, like this one.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.440
Let's assume this angle is theta.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.140
The side opposite to the right angle is called the hypotenuse.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.660
And the other two sides

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.320
are named with respect to the position of this angle.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.140
As this side is right next to the angle,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.440
it's called the adjacent side.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.100
This side is called the opposite side

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.960
as it lies exactly opposite to our reference angle.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.940
Please make sure you understand clearly

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.740
how the sides of the triangles are named.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.180
This is the triangle we will be frequently referring to.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.800
Adjacent is the side right next to the reference angle.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.880
And opposite is the side opposite the reference angle.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.880
Now we are ready to understand the sine function.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.000
We will look at the sine of our reference angle.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.700
The sine of angle theta, is written as sine theta.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.760
Observe that we do not write the 'e'.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.340
sine theta will always equal the opposite

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.980
which is this side divided by the hypotenuse.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.060
Each of these sides will have a length.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.840
So the sine of this angle gives us a numerical value.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.660
Let's see an actual example.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.040
We have this right triangle.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.680
Let this angle be theta.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.660
And let the lengths of the sides be three, four and five units.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.120
The formula for sine theta is opposite by hypotenuse.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.220
The length of the side opposite the angle theta is three units,

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.240
so we write a three in the numerator.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.720
The hypotenuse is 5 units, so we write five in the denominator.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.700
The sine of theta in this case is equal to 3 by 5 .

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.320
Which equals zero point six units.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.580
That's how simple trigonometry is.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.520
All we need to know is what the sides of the right triangle are called.

